---- MODULE spec ----
\* Generated by `spk compile` from spec `spec` — source of truth is the
\* spec file; edit there, not here. Extends nothing: the module is
\* self-contained so any engine can open it.

\* Each State becomes a value in the state variable's range.
StateValues == {"bare", "prepared", "gated", "advised"}

VARIABLES vpc   \* the state variable (program counter)

vars == <<vpc>>

TypeOK == vpc \in StateValues

\* Initial state: first listed in the spec (the format has no explicit initial marker).
Init == vpc = "bare"

Next ==
  \* t-init: bare -> prepared (guard: [[spec.C-init-command]])
  \/ vpc = "bare" /\ vpc' = "prepared"
  \* t-check: prepared -> gated (guard: [[spec.C-check-command]] ([[spec.C-lint-command]] widens quality scope))
  \/ vpc = "prepared" /\ vpc' = "gated"
  \* t-doctor: prepared -> advised (guard: [[spec.C-doctor-command]] ([[spec.C-doctor-enable]] and [[spec.C-recommendation-findings]] refine it))
  \/ vpc = "prepared" /\ vpc' = "advised"
  \* t-lifecycle: prepared -> prepared (guard: [[spec.C-scenario-lifecycle]] AND [[spec.C-archive-companion]] AND [[spec.C-upgrade-command]])
  \/ vpc = "prepared" /\ vpc' = "prepared"
  \* t-guidance: advised -> advised (guard: [[spec.C-type-commands]] AND [[spec.C-explain-subcommand]] AND [[spec.C-report-command]])
  \/ vpc = "advised" /\ vpc' = "advised"
  \* stuttering: guards are prose (uninterpreted) — a terminal
  \* state must not read as an engine-side deadlock
  \/ UNCHANGED vpc

\* No state carries an `emits` field — Output is simply empty.
Output == << >>

